    <h1>2. Operator Guide: Administrator Portal</h1>
    <p>The Admin Dashboard (/admin) serves as the primary administration cockpit. Administrators can review school statistics, manage class records, edit baseline year data, export the database, and configure AI parameters.</p>

    <h2>2.1 Stats Cards & School Year Selection</h2>
    <p>The top cards display real-time school statistics for the active school year. Select a school year from the dropdown list on the upper-right corner of the dashboard to display historical statistics (such as S.Y. 2025-2026 or S.Y. 2021-2022). Dashboard values are recalculated automatically:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Total Enrollment:</span> The sum of active students currently registered in the database for the active year.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Total Dropouts:</span> The count of students flagged with the 'Dropped' status, indicating unenrollment.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Active Faculty:</span> The total number of teacher accounts assigned to the school year roster.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Infrastructure:</span> Indicators summarizing repeaters and physical infrastructure capacity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2.2 Updating School Year & Census Metrics</h2>
    <p>To modify school statistics or class structures:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Click the <span class="strong-term">'Edit Year Statistics'</span> button near the top statistics display.</li>
      <li>A modal will open, displaying grade levels (Kinder to Grade 6). Enter the enrollment, repeater counts, dropout counts, classrooms count, and seats capacity.</li>
      <li>Modify the values for the grades and click <span class="strong-term">'Save Changes'</span>. The portal updates the spreadsheet, and metrics recalculate immediately.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="note">
      <strong>💡 NOTE:</strong> Use the 'Compare Years' feature to view multi-year growth lines, bar charts, and monthly event logs detailing typhoon shifts or school event timelines.
    </div>

    <h2>2.3 Student & Teacher Registries</h2>
    <p>To manage student and teacher details, select the Student or Faculty tab from the sidebar:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Adding a Record:</span> Click '+ Add Student' or '+ Add Teacher' to open the registration forms. Enter the required registry data (LRN, grade level, section, parent details, phone, email, etc.) and submit.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Modifying Status:</span> Toggle the student status dropdown in the registry table from 'Enrolled' to 'Dropped' to instantly update the enrollment stats card.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Deleting a Record:</span> Click 'Delete' next to a row to permanently remove a record from the database sheets.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2.4 Excel Import / Export Tools</h2>
    <p>To perform bulk data operations, click 'Database Tool' in the Admin sidebar:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Backup Database:</span> Click 'Export Database' to compile and download all system registries, grading sheets, and configurations into a structured Excel workbook.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Roster Template:</span> Click 'Download Template' to download a clean Excel sheet formatted to matching Department of Education standards.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Bulk Import:</span> Upload an updated census sheet via the 'Import Census File' button to quickly refresh baseline statistics.</li>
    </ul>

    <h1>3. Operator Guide: Teacher Portal</h1>
    <p>The Teacher Dashboard (/teacher/dashboard) is tailored for classroom instruction. It displays only information relevant to the teacher's grade assignment (e.g. Grade 1 - Mabini).</p>

    <h2>3.1 Student Grades Management</h2>
    <p>To enter or update student quarterly marks:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Select the <span class="strong-term">'Students'</span> tab from the Teacher sidebar to display your section roster.</li>
      <li>Click on a student's name in the table to display their detailed grading sheet.</li>
      <li>The grid displays subjects (Math, Science, English, Filipino, MAPEH, Makabayan) across Q1, Q2, Q3, and Q4 columns. Double-click or select an input box to edit the grade (0 to 100).</li>
      <li>Click <span class="strong-term">'Save Changes'</span> to execute database updates, recalculate averages, and update student summaries.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>3.2 Leaderboard & Exam Schedulers</h2>
    <p>The default tab features advice cards next to a class Leaderboard. The leaderboard ranks students based on their overall quarterly average. To schedule exams, navigate to the 'Exams' tab and click '+ Create Exam' to log titles, schedules, and question formats.</p>

    <h1>4. Operator Guide: Student/Parent Portal</h1>
    <p>The Student Dashboard (/student/dashboard) is designed for students and parents. It offers an easy-to-use academic console:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Subject Proficiency Overview:</span> Reflects the cumulative academic performance of the student. Subjects are automatically categorized: Mastered (Green, avg >= 90), On Track (Yellow, avg 80-89), and Needs Attention (Red, avg < 80).</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Grades & Progress Grid:</span> The main table displays subjects, teacher names, completed quarters, progress bars, and academic standing labels.</li>
      <li><span class="strong-term">Specialized Services:</span> Use navigation tabs to review detailed quarter-by-quarter grids, download award certificates, review monthly attendance logs, check medical records, and submit report card request forms.</li>
    </ul>
    
</body>
</html>

  